 ## Overview
-Octree-based traversal accelerates rendering by recursively navigating a hierarchical spatial subdivision (octree) to skip empty or low-detail regions, thereby reducing the number of intersection tests and sampling operations . It solves the performance bottleneck of dense voxel traversal by allowing rays to take larger steps through empty space . Unlike [Hierarchical Grid Traversal](2560-hierarchical-grid-traversal.md) which uses fixed-level mipmap grids, this family explicitly uses regular 2x2x2 (or 2x2 in 2D) subdivision to build a sparse hierarchy, distinguishing it from siblings that may focus on hash grids or specific traversal optimizations .
